Review comment:

- [P2] Bind the storage assertion to the second page's report — /Volumes/Macintosh HD - Daten/Cloud/Projekte/Apps/Plattformuebergreifend/AhoiBrowser/.work/agent-queue/mobile-files-main-20261006/apps/AhoiMobile/Tests/AhoiMobileUITests/MobileWebExtensionSpikeUITests.swift:47-50
  When the second navigation is slow, `openExamplePage` can return while the first document remains visible: the address can reflect the provisional URL, and both documents have the same title. This selector then accepts the first page's report. Its visit count can already be at least 2 because the extension also runs on the initial fixture, so the storage assertion passes without executing the second page's content script. Include the navigation token in the report, wait for the second token, and compare its count against the first report rather than a fixed minimum.
